<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FNB half yr shr, div rises.[CORRECTED 15:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>FNB half yr shr, div rises.[CORRECTED 15:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended March 31</p>
<p>		    (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    110.4	   vs 103.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     25.0	   vs  20.0</p>
<p>    Retained income	    474.1	   vs 363.6</p>
<p>(Correcting figure of retained income) </p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings rising to between 109.0 and 115.9 cents a share with consensus at 112.0 cents. They expected a dividend of between 21.8 and 23.0 cents with consensus at 22.3.</p>
<p>    Net interest income	1,657.7	 vs  1,570.9</p>
<p>    Other operating income   1,506.4	 vs  1,221.8</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge  (363.9)	vs   (221.2)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  757.6	 vs    736.9</p>
<p>Tax</p>
<p>- non-recurring</p>
<p>    operations		     47.9	  vs     -</p>
<p>Div payable around June 9 1997</p>
<p>On register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: First National Bank Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
